    // picture (a country's flag) meant the picture. But only a URL that
    // survives `_safeMediaUrl` — the one gate every <img> in this file goes
    // through — and only an image one: an <img> cannot show data:video, so
    // accepting it would draw the browser's broken-image box. A refused URL
    // falls through to the icon, dot or initials (`_optionGlyph`) rather
    // than leaving the slot empty, so a list whose flags come from
    // somewhere untrusted degrades to its glyphs instead of to gaps — and
    // so, below, does a URL that passes the gate and then fails to load.
