        // engine. Each draws a failed <img> its own way: Chromium an empty
        // gap, Firefox and WebKit a hollow grey-bordered box — in every row
        // of a two-hundred-country list and on the trigger, whenever the
        // flag host answers 403 or is unreachable. The listener goes on
        // BEFORE `src`, so there is no moment in which the image can fail
        // with nobody listening.
