  //: What stands in for an option's picture once it has failed: the
  //: option's own icon, dot or avatar when it has one — the same fallback a
  //: URL the gate refuses gets — and otherwise an EMPTY BOX the picture's
  //: size. Empty rather than nothing, so a row whose flag failed keeps its
  //: label in line with the rows whose flags arrived; a span, so no engine
  //: has a broken image to draw a border or a glyph for. It carries the
  //: picture's own class, which is what gives it the size (and the larger
  //: size in a `size="lg"` field).
